@page "/"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject IRomaniaEFacturaService EFactura

<PageTitle>e-Factura sample</PageTitle>

<h1>Romanian e-Factura</h1>

<p class="lead">
    Every method on <code>IRomaniaEFacturaService</code>, reachable from a page. This app is the
    library's documentation as much as its demonstration.
</p>

@if (_status is not null && !_status.IsConnected)
{
    <div class="alert alert-warning">
        <strong>Not authorized.</strong> Nothing can be sent or downloaded for CIF
        @_status.Cif until someone authorizes it — <a href="/connect">start here</a>.
    </div>
}

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Registration</h2>
<pre class="border rounded p-3 bg-body-tertiary"><code>builder.AddRomaniaEFactura(
    configureDatabase: options =&gt; options.UseSqlite(connectionString));

app.MapEFacturaAuthorization();</code></pre>

<p>
    That is the whole setup. Options bind from the <code>EFactura</code> configuration section;
    inject <code>IRomaniaEFacturaService</code> wherever you need it.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Running against the mock</h2>
<p>
    <code>appsettings.json</code> points <code>ApiBaseAddress</code> and
    <code>OAuthBaseAddress</code> at <code>MockAnafServer</code>. Start that project first, or
    remove both settings to talk to ANAF's real test environment — nothing else changes.
</p>

<h2 class="h4 mt-4">Where to look</h2>
<ul>
    <li><a href="/connect">Connection</a> — the authorize flow, and the "not authorized yet" state.</li>
    <li><a href="/invoices/new">New invoice</a> — the edit model, live derived totals, BR-coded verification.</li>
    <li><a href="/other">Credit notes &amp; messages</a> — credit note, buyer message, raw XML escape hatch.</li>
    <li><a href="/submissions">Sent</a> — what the background reconciler has established.</li>
    <li><a href="/inbox">Inbox</a> — watermark sync, discriminated documents, archive and PDF.</li>
</ul>

@code {
    private AuthorizationStatus? _status;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() =>
        _status = await EFactura.GetAuthorizationStatusAsync();
}
